  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Indigenous-Quilombola Alliance in Oriximin&#xe1;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Contribute to increased protagonism of indigenous and quilombolas in Oriximin&#xe1; in the defence of their rights and the promotion of a sustainable life through strengthening of the capacity of the representative organizations that make up the Oriximin&#xe1; indigenous-quilombola alliance. Promote activities specifically targeting quilombola, indigenous and riverine women in Oriximin&#xe1; and &#xd3;bidos through a permanent agenda of training and mobilization on topics defined jointly with the female beneficiaries. Expanded ability of the residents of 11 guarani villages inside the Pia&#xe7;aguera land to promote territorial and environmental management. Expand CPI-SP&#x2019;s capacity to adopt a gender approach in its various activities, in addition to strengthened policies to promote diversity, equity and inclusion within the organization.</narrative>
  </description>
